  "solution": {
    "text": "Isoelectronic species have same no. of electrons. Below are the isoelectronic species with their respective no. of electrons:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>Sc</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>18</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>18</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>18</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>18</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><br />All of the above elements have the electronic configuration of argon.",
